[{"id": "17592186176259-after", "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with a joint probability density function\n\n$f(x, y) = \\frac{1}{2}xy, 0 \\le x \\le y \\le 2$.\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF $f_{X}(x)$.", "solution": "", "fields": [{"id": "17592186173812", "key": "selection", "type": "radio", "choices": [{"id": "17592186173813", "type": "text", "value": "${f}_{X} ( x ) = \\left\\{  \\begin{array}{ll}\\frac{1}{10} x + \\frac{1}{5} {x}^{3} , & 0 \\le  x \\le  2 , \\\\ 0 , & \\text{otherwise} .\\end{array} \\right$."}, {"id": "17592186173814", "type": "text", "value": "${f}_{X} ( x ) = \\left\\{  \\begin{array}{ll}x - \\frac{1}{4} {x}^{3} , & 0 \\le  x \\le  2 , \\\\ 0 , & \\text{otherwise} .\\end{array} \\right$."}, {"id": "17592186173815", "type": "text", "value": "${f}_{X} ( x ) = \\left\\{  \\begin{array}{ll}{x}^{2} + \\frac{1}{4} {x}^{3} , & 0 \\le  x \\le  2 , \\\\ 0 , & \\text{otherwise} .\\end{array} \\right$."}, {"id": "17592186173816", "type": "text", "value": "${f}_{X} ( x ) = \\left\\{  \\begin{array}{ll}\\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{5} {x}^{3} , & 0 \\le  x \\le  2 , \\\\ 0 , & \\text{otherwise} .\\end{array} \\right$."}, {"id": "17592186173817", "type": "text", "value": "${f}_{X} ( x ) = \\left\\{  \\begin{array}{ll}2 {x}^{2} - \\frac{1}{4} {x}^{3} , & 0 \\le  x \\le  2 , \\\\ 0 , & \\text{otherwise} .\\end{array} \\right$."}]}], "omitTrees": true, "screenshot": false}, {"id": "17592186176397-after", "problem": "![](images/bc/bc0e25e290235560cca0c2c0f18b8b22a8f1909e29c1d8706fff6cfc3ca8955a.png)\n\nThe solid enclosed by the quarter-sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9$ for $y\\ge 0$ and $x\\le 0,$ shown above, can be described in spherical polar coordinates as", "solution": "We write the position of a point (vector) in spherical polar coordinates as $(\\rho ,\\theta ,\u03d5),$ where \n\n- $\\rho \\ge 0$ is the distance from the point to the origin,\n\n- $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$ is the angle between the point and the positive $x$-axis, and\n\n- $\u03d5\\in [0,\\pi ]$ is the angle the corresponding vector makes with the positive $z$-axis.\n\n![](images/e3/e33bd1b452217ea524c15bc6fc9555c6e12cd07e929e8aa473ce6e3db1322f0e.png)\n\n  \n\nNotice that inside our region, the spherical polar coordinates vary withing the following domains:\n\n- $\\rho \\in [0,3]$\n\n- $\\theta \\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]$\n\n- $\u03d5\\in [0,\\pi ]$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{(\\rho ,\\theta ,\u03d5)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 3,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le \u03d5\\le \\pi }.\n$$", "fields": [{"id": "17592186174640", "key": "selection", "type": "radio", "choices": [{"id": "17592186174641", "type": "math", "value": "{(\u03c1, \u03b8, \u03d5): 0 \\le \u03c1 \\le 9, 0 \\le \u03b8 \\le \u03c0, 0 \\le \u03d5 \\le 2 \u03c0}"}, {"id": "17592186174642", "type": "math", "value": "\\{  ( \\rho  , \\theta  , \\varphi  ) \\hspace{0.167em} : \\hspace{0.167em} 0 \\le  \\rho  \\le  \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{9} , \\hspace{0.222em} \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{- \\frac{\\pi }{2}} \\le  \\theta  \\le  \\pi  , \\hspace{0.222em} 0 \\le  \\varphi  \\le  \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\pi} \\}"}, {"id": "17592186174643", "type": "math", "value": "\\{  ( \\rho  , \\theta  , \\varphi  ) \\hspace{0.167em} : \\hspace{0.167em} 0 \\le  \\rho  \\le  \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{3} , \\hspace{0.222em} \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\frac{\\pi }{2}} \\le  \\theta  \\le  \\pi  , \\hspace{0.222em} 0 \\le  \\varphi  \\le  \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{2 \\pi} \\}"}, {"id": "17592186174644", "type": "math", "value": "{(\u03c1, \u03b8, \u03d5): 0 \\le \u03c1 \\le 3, 0 \\le \u03b8 \\le \u03c0, 0 \\le \u03d5 \\le \u03c0}"}, {"id": "17592186174645", "type": "math", "value": "\\{  ( \\rho  , \\theta  , \\varphi  ) \\hspace{0.167em} : \\hspace{0.167em} 0 \\le  \\rho  \\le  \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{3} , \\hspace{0.222em} \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\frac{\\pi }{2}} \\le  \\theta  \\le  \\pi  , \\hspace{0.222em} 0 \\le  \\varphi  \\le  \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\pi} \\}"}]}, {"id": "17592186363425", "key": "selection", "type": "radio", "choices": [{"id": "17592186363426", "type": "math", "value": "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,\u03d5)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 3,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le \u03d5\\le \\pi }"}, {"id": "17592186363427", "type": "math", "value": "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,\u03d5)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 3,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le \u03d5\\le \\pi }"}, {"id": "17592186363428", "type": "math", "value": "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,\u03d5)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 3,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le \u03d5\\le 2\\pi }"}, {"id": "17592186363429", "type": "math", "value": "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,\u03d5)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 9,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le \u03d5\\le 2\\pi }"}, {"id": "17592186363430", "type": "math", "value": "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,\u03d5)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 9,\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le \u03d5\\le \\pi }"}]}], "omitTrees": true, "screenshot": false}, {"id": "17592186176399-after", "problem": "![](images/d2/d27f12d8891ca49a1b59de45506a55885a58236e5ea94c54a97cb22cf33ba982.png)\n\nThe solid enclosed by the quarter-sphere $x^{2} + y^{2} + z^{2} = 18y$ for $x \\ge 0$ and $z \\ge 0$, shown above, can be described in spherical polar coordinates as", "solution": "", "fields": [{"id": "17592186174652", "key": "selection", "type": "radio", "choices": [{"id": "17592186174653", "type": "math", "value": "{(\u03c1, \u03b8, \u03d5): 0 \\le \u03c1 \\le 18, 0 \\le \u03b8 \\le 2 \u03c0, 0 \\le \u03d5 \\le \u03c0}"}, {"id": "17592186174654", "type": "math", "value": "{(\u03c1, \u03b8, \u03d5): 0 \\le \u03c1 \\le 9 cos \u2061 \u03b8 sin \u2061 \u03d5, 0 \\le \u03b8 \\le \u03c0, 0 \\le \u03d5 \\le \u03c0}"}, {"id": "17592186174655", "type": "math", "value": "\\{  ( \\rho  , \\theta  , \\varphi  ) \\hspace{0.167em} : \\hspace{0.167em} 0 \\le  \\rho  \\le  \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{18 \\cos   \\theta  \\sin   \\varphi} , \\hspace{0.222em} 0 \\le  \\theta  \\le  \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\frac{\\pi }{2}} , \\hspace{0.222em} 0 \\le  \\varphi  \\le  \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\frac{\\pi }{2}} \\}"}, {"id": "17592186174656", "type": "math", "value": "\\{  ( \\rho  , \\theta  , \\varphi  ) \\hspace{0.167em} : \\hspace{0.167em} 0 \\le  \\rho  \\le  \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{9} , \\hspace{0.222em} 0 \\le  \\theta  \\le  \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\pi} , \\hspace{0.222em} 0 \\le  \\varphi  \\le  \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\frac{\\pi }{2}} \\}"}, {"id": "17592186174657", "type": "math", "value": "\\{  ( \\rho  , \\theta  , \\varphi  ) \\hspace{0.167em} : \\hspace{0.167em} 0 \\le  \\rho  \\le  \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{18 \\sin   \\theta  \\sin   \\varphi} , \\hspace{0.222em} 0 \\le  \\theta  \\le  \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\frac{\\pi }{2}} , \\hspace{0.222em} 0 \\le  \\varphi  \\le  \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\frac{\\pi }{2}} \\}"}]}], "omitTrees": true, "screenshot": true}]
